WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.160
Hello and welcome back to JD Science.

2
00:00:02.720 --> 00:00:05.340
Today we are exploring plant disease.

3
00:00:06.060 --> 00:00:10.380
Signs of disease include stunted growth, spots on leaves, areas

4
00:00:10.380 --> 00:00:14.120
of decay, growths, pests and discoloured

5
00:00:14.120 --> 00:00:15.420
or misshapen leaves.

6
00:00:16.080 --> 00:00:19.780
Rose black spot is a fungal disease that causes black spots on

7
00:00:19.780 --> 00:00:22.620
leaves which turn yellow and fall early.

8
00:00:23.060 --> 00:00:24.980
It spreads by wind and rain.

9
00:00:24.980 --> 00:00:28.600
Tobacco mosaic virus causes mosaic patterns on

10
00:00:28.600 --> 00:00:30.820
leaves and reduces photosynthesis.

11
00:00:31.580 --> 00:00:35.240
Nitrate deficiency causes stunted growth because nitrates

12
00:00:35.240 --> 00:00:36.440
are needed for protein.

13
00:00:37.080 --> 00:00:40.860
Magnesium deficiency causes chlorosis because magnesium is

14
00:00:40.860 --> 00:00:42.320
needed, to make chlorophyll.

15
00:00:43.140 --> 00:00:47.000
Plants defend themselves with physical barriers like waxy cuticles and

16
00:00:47.000 --> 00:00:51.080
thorns and chemical defences such as antibacterial chemicals.

17
00:00:51.820 --> 00:00:55.560
Mineral deficiencies can resemble infectious diseases, so the pattern

18
00:00:55.560 --> 00:00:56.660
of symptoms matters.

19
00:00:57.260 --> 00:01:00.960
Magnesium deficiency commonly causes intervenal chlorosis,

20
00:01:01.400 --> 00:01:05.200
particularly in older species because magnesium is a mobile

21
00:01:05.200 --> 00:01:07.680
nutrient and is required for chlorophyll.

22
00:01:08.300 --> 00:01:12.080
Nitrate deficiency can cause poor growth because nitrogen is needed

23
00:01:12.080 --> 00:01:14.260
to make amino acids and proteins.

24
00:01:14.260 --> 00:01:18.220
A plant's appearance is evidence, but careful diagnosis

25
00:01:18.220 --> 00:01:20.160
may require further investigation.

26
00:01:20.820 --> 00:01:24.420
As you revise this topic, try to explain the key process

27
00:01:24.420 --> 00:01:25.680
in your own words.

28
00:01:26.100 --> 00:01:29.900
Focus on what happens, why it happens and how the structures

29
00:01:29.900 --> 00:01:31.800
involved help the process work.

30
00:01:32.280 --> 00:01:35.920
Now pause the video and try this exam style question.

31
00:01:36.440 --> 00:01:39.220
A plant has yellow leaves with green veins.

32
00:01:39.860 --> 00:01:43.380
Suggest which mineral ion is missing and explain your answer.

33
00:01:43.840 --> 00:01:45.020
Here is a model answer.

34
00:01:45.520 --> 00:01:46.140
Magnesium.

35
00:01:46.780 --> 00:01:50.740
It is needed to make chlorophyll, so a deficiency causes chlorosis

36
00:01:50.740 --> 00:01:51.380
yellowing.

37
00:01:51.760 --> 00:01:55.440
If this explanation has helped, please subscribe to JD Science

38
00:01:55.440 --> 00:01:56.460
for more lessons.

39
00:01:57.100 --> 00:02:00.800
You can find further learning resources and practice questions at

40
00:02:00.800 --> 00:02:05.180
jdsciense .co

41
00:02:05.180 --> 00:02:05.920
.uk.

42
00:02:06.480 --> 00:02:07.360
Thank you for watching.
